{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 783 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "a4ed9229c4956188f9ade8de64817f442d55a8fd128ec1bfa11b1fc0a39568ad" :edb/db-before-t 782 :edb/db-after-t 783 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534095 50 #inst "2026-10-06T02:51:41.542Z" 13194139534095 true] [17592186064282 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277471 13194139534095 true] [17592186064282 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277474 13194139534095 true] [17592186064282 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277483 13194139534095 true] [17592186064283 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277480 13194139534095 true] [17592186064856 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534095 true] [17592186064856 1100 "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nThe position $s(t)$ of a particle (in centimeters) at time $t$ seconds is given by\n$s(t) = \\frac{5t - 10}{t}, t > 0$.\nCalculate the speed of the particle when $t = 2s$." 13194139534095 false] [17592186064856 1100 "The position $s(t)$ of a particle (in centimeters) at time $t$ seconds is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)=\\frac{5t-10}{t},\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle when $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$" 13194139534095 true] [17592186064856 1145 "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{5t-10}{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $t=2,$ the velocity is\n\n$$\nv(2)=\\frac{10}{(2)^{2}}=\\frac{10}{4}=2.5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed is $|2.5|=2.5\\,\\text{cm/s}.$" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277471 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277472 13194139534095 true] [17592186277471 1089 "q-336138" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277471 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534095 true] [17592186277471 1100 "The position $x$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by \n\n$$\nx(t)=16\\sqrt{t}-{t}^{4},\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity at time $t=1.$\n\n$v(1)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277471 1113 #uuid "f31d851b-1815-542f-834c-0040330b3a50" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277471 1145 "The velocity is the derivative of the position function $x(t)$ with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(16\\sqrt{t}-{t}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{2\\sqrt{t}}-4{t}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{t}}-4{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=1,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{1}}-4({1}^{3}) \\\\  & =8-4 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277472 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277473 13194139534095 true] [17592186277472 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534095 true] [17592186277472 1041 "field-1" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277472 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277473 13194139534095 true] [17592186277472 1110 #uuid "2531ee74-f8b3-5fee-89f8-3afeb7eea38a" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277473 1034 "4" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277473 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534095 true] [17592186277473 1111 #uuid "4f8d490f-d676-5edc-9479-5ffe2d436b48" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277474 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277475 13194139534095 true] [17592186277474 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277478 13194139534095 true] [17592186277474 1089 "q-336166" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277474 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534095 true] [17592186277474 1100 "The displacement $s$ (in meters) relative to a fixed origin $O$ of a particle moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis is given by the equation $s(t)=\\frac{{2}^{t}}{{2}^{t}+1}$, where $t$ is the time, measured in seconds. Find the position ${s}_{0}$ and velocity ${v}_{0}$ of the particle at the initial moment of time $t=0\\,\\text{s}.$\n\n${s}_{0}=$\n{{field-1}}$\\text{m}\\,\\text{and}\\,$\n\n${v}_{0}=$\n{{field-2}}$\\text{m/s}$" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277474 1113 #uuid "3c9f7bfd-dd97-5c50-bff1-b05200e8ca4e" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277474 1145 "To calculate the initial position, we substitute $t=0$ it into the equation $s(t)=\\frac{{2}^{t}}{{2}^{t}+1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{0} & =s(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{0}}{{2}^{0}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{2}^{t}}{{2}^{t}+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{({2}^{t}+1)\\cdot {2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-{2}^{t}\\cdot {2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{({2}^{t}+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{({2}^{t}+1)}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=0\\,\\text{s},$ we substitute $t=0$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{0} & =v(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{0}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{({2}^{0}+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{4}\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277475 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277476 13194139534095 true] [17592186277475 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277477 13194139534095 true] [17592186277475 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534095 true] [17592186277475 1041 "field-1" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277475 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277476 13194139534095 true] [17592186277475 1110 #uuid "1f6d8522-b08f-5cd2-9006-f465e704631f" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277476 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277476 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534095 true] [17592186277476 1111 #uuid "24dc7e9b-39dc-551d-9716-801d255f68c4" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277477 1034 "1" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277477 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534095 true] [17592186277477 1111 #uuid "da56aff1-a846-523b-923e-de795c83da9d" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277478 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277479 13194139534095 true] [17592186277478 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534095 true] [17592186277478 1041 "field-2" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277478 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277479 13194139534095 true] [17592186277478 1110 #uuid "301aa2c1-a7d2-572a-92b2-dbd8c49c98f0" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277479 1034 "\\frac{\\ln(2)}{4}" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277479 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534095 true] [17592186277479 1111 #uuid "6e115967-e80b-52b0-97f9-481c9ee6e3fd" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277480 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277481 13194139534095 true] [17592186277480 1089 "q-336186" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277480 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534095 true] [17592186277480 1100 "The position $s(t)$ of a particle (in inches) at time $t$ minutes is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)=3{t}^{4}-4{e}^{t},\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle when $t=0\\,\\text{min}.$\n\nThe speed of the particle is \n{{field-1}}$\\text{in/min}.$" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277480 1113 #uuid "c1b6e4b2-26cc-5cd3-b616-d286a84f4a20" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277480 1145 "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{4}-4{e}^{t}) \\\\  & =12{t}^{3}-4{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $t=0,$ the velocity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(0) & =12\\cdot {0}^{3}-4{e}^{0} \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed is $|-4|=4\\,\\text{in/min}.$" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277481 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277482 13194139534095 true] [17592186277481 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534095 true] [17592186277481 1041 "field-1" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277481 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277482 13194139534095 true] [17592186277481 1110 #uuid "5ffc2ec4-6b31-5f60-a238-dd3fed91e04d" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277482 1034 "4" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277482 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534095 true] [17592186277482 1111 #uuid "76444ab8-3205-5dd4-8465-39fd1fb69557" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277483 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277484 13194139534095 true] [17592186277483 1089 "q-7169" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277483 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534095 true] [17592186277483 1100 "The position $x$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $x(t)={t}^{2}(2t+4).$ Calculate the velocity at time $t=2.$" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277483 1113 #uuid "1b08d9a6-05a2-5df5-bf4f-68c02807ae8d" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277483 1145 "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[{t}^{2}(2t+4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}+8t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =6(2)^{2}+8(2) \\\\  & =24+16 \\\\  & =40\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277484 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277485 13194139534095 true] [17592186277484 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277486 13194139534095 true] [17592186277484 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277487 13194139534095 true] [17592186277484 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277488 13194139534095 true] [17592186277484 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277489 13194139534095 true] [17592186277484 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534095 true] [17592186277484 1041 "selection" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277484 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277486 13194139534095 true] [17592186277484 1110 #uuid "4468bb8b-dd7a-57fe-9f12-205030ccafa1" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277485 1034 "v=32" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277485 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534095 true] [17592186277485 1111 #uuid "d11c166b-c962-56da-8e30-d05daf2adfea" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277486 1034 "v=40" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277486 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534095 true] [17592186277486 1111 #uuid "978c361e-3372-5458-98de-c138327c51cf" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277487 1034 "v=38" 13194139534095 true] [17592186277487 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534095 true] [17592186277487 1111 #uuid "2029c861-e843-5d75-8f0c-e981f19